**Part A** — every shape/rule in the five interface docs checked against its producing/consuming code. 12 mismatches, all indexed at the top with `doc:line vs code:line`:
- Real behavior drift: `recommend._rank` orders starter-tier before params and only within `comfortable` rows, against the Pick rule's text (:80-82) — which of the two is intent needs Jason's word.
- Stale doc: the hardening pip argv block omits `--no-deps` (code and the doc's own prose have it); measurement-core's concurrency count says "the two without one" (three with MTPLX), its sample result dict misses `pid`/`interval_s`, and its header pin list omits `quick`.
- Shape/label drift in v5-app: `.exited(status, stderrTail)` vs the `onExit` closure, "Stop After This Cell"/"Stop Now" title case, "Check Again".
- Minor: `lab_paths(read=)` seam, unenforced "only query parameter", `run(abort=)` missing from the quickbench signature block, `cards`/`cells` naming.

**Part B** — 263 tests examined (the 7 most-recently-changed files = 249, past the ≥200 boundary, plus 3 same-date Swift files); 2 flagged, each re-read against its production code before listing: `test_server.py::test_recommendations_leaves_measured_here_null_without_a_finished_quick_run` (assertion decided by the fake's own `best: None`; passes with the fill deleted) and `AppModelTests.swift::testExcludedModelCarriesItsReason` (assertions echo the stub's own constants through a verbatim assignment).

